{"w":2400,"h":3395,"lines":[{"c":1,"t":"Reading","y":0.11261886559640821,"w":0.072931092580159507,"h":0.015185174166945536,"x":0.83503228315784028},{"t":"READING","c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074,"x":0.47736625347131789,"y":0.15552325567058833,"w":0.12139918009440109},{"c":1,"y":0.20784883707247559,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","x":0.17901234321258708,"w":0.2654321034749349,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"w":0.71203709920247404,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","y":0.23821840463038146,"x":0.17896619854348528,"h":0.018662299930136683,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.25581395335690194,"t":"Passage 1 below.","x":0.18106995611085039,"w":0.14197531382242842,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"t":"C","x":0.17695473255946514,"w":0.016460905075073251,"y":0.62645348818454427,"h":0.011627907185728592,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.2906360426300777,"h":0.017503492402524912,"t":"The concept of intelligence","x":0.39711933531259985,"w":0.29012346903483072},{"y":0.32110368387950194,"w":0.69358688354492193,"x":0.21392803111720943,"c":1,"t":"Looked at in one way, everyone knows what intelligence is; looked at in another way, no one","h":0.018299083125605242},{"w":0.67305440266927075,"y":0.33564495891672885,"h":0.01971891378485835,"x":0.21798914900554686,"t":"does. In other words, people all have unconscious notions - known as 'implicit theories' -","c":1},{"x":0.22009301658880645,"w":0.67709218343098965,"t":"of intelligence, but no one knows for certain what it actually is. This chapter addresses how","h":0.016148156075090125,"c":1,"y":0.35196682407628654},{"h":0.017959786809375267,"c":1,"y":0.36848503081656281,"t":"people conceptualize intelligence, whatever it may actually be.","w":0.46935404459635421,"x":0.21797912183514256},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"y":0.39244186032864026,"c":1,"x":0.22016459999658081,"t":"But why should we even care what people think intelligence is, as opposed only to valuing","w":0.67078191121419273},{"c":1,"t":"whatever it actually is? There are at least four reasons people's conceptions of intelligence","x":0.22010963618126311,"y":0.4073538684812541,"h":0.016030791229859065,"w":0.66883890787760414},{"w":0.67295944213867187,"x":0.21599757769736716,"y":0.44585764584217946,"c":1,"t":"First, implicit theories of intelligence drive the way in which people perceive and evaluate","h":0.01793657287130368},{"t":"their own intelligence and that of others. To better understand the judgments people make","y":0.46366279057807036,"c":1,"x":0.2201646089496497,"w":0.66666666666666663,"h":0.013081395583944611},{"t":"about their own and others' abilities, it is useful to learn about people's implicit theories.","c":1,"w":0.65843622843424476,"y":0.47819767428430038,"h":0.01453488398216074,"x":0.22016460176436947},{"y":0.49268823151132146,"t":"For example, parents' implicit theories of their children's language development will","x":0.21805124551564917,"w":0.62975341796875006,"h":0.01720036831284022,"c":1},{"w":0.6667728169759114,"c":1,"h":0.015571512238016116,"y":0.50849172780459262,"t":"determine at what ages they will be willing to make various corrections in their children's","x":0.22012036520533884},{"h":0.016472727727272152,"c":1,"t":"speech. More generally, parents' implicit theories of intelligence will determine at what ages","y":0.5233428523071304,"w":0.68737009684244799,"x":0.22009856780593565},{"y":0.54063604266147114,"x":0.21810698855955699,"c":1,"t":"they believe their children are ready to perform various cognitive tasks. Job interviewers","w":0.65843622843424487,"h":0.014723203769140158},{"y":0.5542459037452,"w":0.64827672322591146,"t":"will make hiring decisions on the basis of their implicit theories of intelligence. People","h":0.017335366584948608,"x":0.21804506886639008,"c":1},{"t":"will decide who to be friends with on the basis of such theories. In sum, knowledge about","y":0.57122093009881036,"x":0.2201646089798851,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"w":0.66666666666666663},{"h":0.01696618061043198,"y":0.58552073273578642,"w":0.65238703409830723,"c":1,"x":0.21804650954367408,"t":"implicit theories of intelligence is important because this knowledge is so often used by"},{"w":0.4732510375976563,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1,"t":"people to make judgments in the course of their everyday lives.","x":0.21810699138790804,"y":0.60306242664155962},{"x":0.21604938175751537,"c":1,"t":"Second, the implicit theories of scientific investigators ultimately give rise to their explicit","w":0.67283950805664072,"h":0.016048292108362783,"y":0.6249999998515362},{"h":0.014534883982160851,"c":1,"x":0.22016462199542597,"y":0.64098837195499225,"w":0.63786005655924483,"t":"theories. Thus it is useful to find out what these implicit theories are. Implicit theories"},{"w":0.62345677693684898,"x":0.21810700236391048,"h":0.014562276002234587,"y":0.65694935203229088,"t":"provide a framework that is useful in defining the general scope of a phenomenon -","c":1},{"h":0.016413699892581013,"t":"especially a not-well-understood phenomenon. These implicit theories can suggest what","w":0.65446619669596351,"c":1,"x":0.22009811580702471,"y":0.67062840794058942},{"h":0.015529843747124294,"y":0.68684269951693022,"w":0.6605964660644531,"x":0.2201123598720299,"c":1,"t":"aspects of the phenomenon have been more or less attended to in previous investigations."},{"y":0.70923707764394506,"h":0.017450726916849013,"x":0.21804100508986379,"t":"Third, implicit theories can be useful when an investigator suspects that existing explicit","w":0.65859354654947921,"c":1},{"t":"theories are wrong or misleading. If an investigation of implicit theories reveals little","y":0.72673733831624565,"x":0.21810699233295036,"w":0.63374486287434895,"h":0.015995219964161089,"c":1},{"x":0.22016460801337548,"h":0.013250883392226132,"t":"correspondence between the extant implicit and explicit theories, the implicit theories may","y":0.74263839812602317,"w":0.67283950805664061,"c":1},{"y":0.75702523490010509,"t":"be wrong. But the possibility also needs to be taken into account that the explicit theories","x":0.22012735499517305,"h":0.01532469930300584,"w":0.66470006306966156,"c":1},{"y":0.77325581383304054,"w":0.62757202148437496,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"t":"are wrong and in need of correction or supplementation. For example, some implicit","x":0.22016460647393463},{"h":0.01472320376914027,"x":0.22016460087448669,"y":0.78769140139667693,"c":1,"w":0.66460906982421863,"t":"theories of intelligence suggest the need for expansion of some of our explicit theories of"},{"x":0.21992445404327468,"y":0.80499208826652857,"t":"the construct.","w":0.10551883697509765,"c":1,"h":0.012041318262142942},{"w":0.024691357612609877,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"t":"59","x":0.88271604948587612,"y":0.86918604632866725}]}